{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe 2026-08-18 operator ruling (signed, recorded on restoring-shallow-blobfish)\nrescinded the older \"force is CLI/library-only\" policy: `--force[=<reason>]` is now\nallowed through EVERY command surface — library, CLI, and MCP. Auditability no longer\ncomes from withholding the capability from MCP; it comes from the ABSENCE of a signed\nattestation. A forced write produces no certification, and projects that want to prevent\nforce from circumventing a gate check for that certification in their CI pipeline.\n\nThe MCP-parity sibling (scratchy-leprous-galago, landed) already exposes reason-bearing\n`force: str | None` on `transition_ticket` and `claim_ticket` and rewrote the tool\ndocstrings to the absent-attestation model. The canonical prose has NOT caught up: two\ndocuments still assert force is CLI-only / not exposed over MCP for the transition+claim\nsurface, contradicting the shipped code. This is a docs-only correction.\n\n## Approach\n\nRewrite the stale transition/claim `--force` prose to the ruling's model in place, without\ntouching code or the already-correct MCP docstrings:\n\n1. AGENTS.md: the start-work-gate `--force[=<reason>]` paragraph ends \"it is CLI-only and\n   not exposed over MCP.\" Replace that clause with the force-everywhere + absent-attestation\n   + CI-certification-enforcement model. Because the Copilot and Claude bridge files import\n   AGENTS.md, this single edit propagates to every harness.\n2. docs/user-guide.md: the `rebar claim <id> --force[=<reason>]` paragraph ends \"`--force`\n   is CLI-only: it is not exposed over MCP (an MCP client always goes through the configured\n   gate).\" Replace with the same force-everywhere + absent-attestation model.\n\nThe edits are scoped strictly to the transition+claim `--force` blast radius named in the\nruling. Unrelated CLI-only statements about OTHER bypass families stay untouched: the\n`--allow-secret-pattern` secret-scan override paragraph in docs/user-guide.md, the\ninteractive `bridge setup` wizard, and the release-notes setup-wizard note are all distinct\nconcepts and out of scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- AGENTS.md — rewrite the trailing CLI-only clause of the start-work `--force` paragraph.\n- docs/user-guide.md — rewrite the trailing CLI-only sentence of the claim `--force`\n  paragraph.\n\nNo code, tests, MCP docstrings (already correct), config, or event-schema changes.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only change with no executable behavior, so there is no unit test to add;\nverification is by inspection and repo-wide grep:\n\n- After the edit, `grep -rni \"cli-only\" AGENTS.md docs/user-guide.md` returns no line that\n  claims the transition or claim `--force` is CLI-only or unavailable over MCP (the\n  surviving matches are the out-of-scope secret-pattern / bridge-setup families).\n- `grep -rni \"not exposed over mcp\" AGENTS.md docs/user-guide.md` returns no transition/claim\n  `--force` match.\n- The rewritten passages state force is available on lib/CLI/MCP, that audit comes from the\n  absent signed attestation, and that CI certification-checks are the enforcement lever.\n- `make lint` stays green (prose-only; no code touched).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AGENTS.md states the transition/claim `--force[=<reason>]` override is available on\n      all surfaces (library, CLI, MCP), not CLI-only.\n- [ ] docs/user-guide.md states the claim `--force` override is exposed over MCP, not\n      CLI-only.\n- [ ] Both rewritten passages describe the absent-signed-attestation audit model and the\n      CI-certification enforcement option.\n- [ ] No remaining claim in AGENTS.md or docs/user-guide.md that the transition or claim\n      `--force` is CLI-only / unavailable over MCP.\n- [ ] Out-of-scope CLI-only statements (secret-pattern override, bridge setup, release-notes\n      wizard) are left unchanged.\n- [ ] The wording is consistent with the shipped MCP surface (scratchy) and the already-\n      updated `_mcp_writes.py` docstrings."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787119211640659001,"uuid":"0bbed48b-d927-4843-b737-2dc840242540"}